<title>UK: New data swells IPAI aluminium capacity estimate.</title>
<headline>New data swells IPAI aluminium capacity estimate.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The inclusion of data from China, Tajikistan and Montenegro for the first time has lifted the International Primary Aluminium Institute's (IPAI) estimate of world aluminium production capacity by the end of the century to 23.138 million tonnes.</p>
<p>On the same basis production capacity at the end of 1996 was 22.207 million tonnes but, before the new data was included, capacity at the end of June 1996 was 19.280 million tonnes, the IPAI data showed.</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
